{
  "note": "Eval cases for agent tools. `expected_tools` is what the agent must call for the question (checked once the agent exists); `checks` run today against the tool output. Cases with `\"agent\": true` are also asked to the live analyst (evals/run_agent.py). `answer_checks` are scored on the recorded answer (evals/checks.py answer_check); a case with no expected tool is a question the analyst should refuse or say it cannot answer. `group` sorts agent cases: refusal, missing_data, language, new_tool, multi_turn. A multi_turn case asks its `earlier_turns` first in one conversation; only `question` is recorded and scored.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "rank-basic",
      "question": "What can I change to cut my machinery emissions?",
      "expected_tools": [
        "rank_interventions"
      ],
      "arguments": {},
      "checks": [
